portdbapi: aux_get() answers from a valid cache entry without the event loop

Sub-series: O (stage 4, round 2) - patch 2 of 3; applies without the other patches of O.
Base: upstream 73646c35d.

aux_get() runs async_aux_get() through run_until_complete(), which costs a task
and two passes of the loop per call, although the coroutine awaits nothing when
the answer is in _aux_cache or the ebuild has a valid metadata cache entry. A
resolve makes several thousand such calls. _aux_get_no_wait() holds the
statements of async_aux_get() up to its first await, in the same order; in every
other case (unknown repository, malformed cpv, ebuild not found, no valid cache
entry) it returns None and aux_get() runs async_aux_get() as before, which
reports the problem or runs the metadata phase.
Maintenance: the two bodies must be kept in step when async_aux_get() changes.

Judge, medians: 0033 and 0034 together on 0001-0031: 88.6 s -> 85.3 s (four
passes); 0033 alone 85.8 against 87.2 s (three passes, inside the noise).
Lock-step counters of the author: 59,743 no-wait answers, 895 fallbacks,
0 mismatches. See 0032 for origin and for why there is no author report.
Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in stage 4 of the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-21, on
upstream commit 73646c35d with patches 0001-0030 and the C modules applied. Not a
human-written change. Judge: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of one system image, six
resolves in parallel, wall seconds summed; every run gave the same merge list in the same
order and the same number of backtracking attempts as unpatched 73646c35d. Black-box
testers (invented states, reference against candidate): 0 differences.

Ported to upstream bdf046b03 (2026-11-23) by a three-way merge per file (base 73646c35d).

